# IF GIT SHOWED THAT THIS FILE CHANGED
#
# 1. RUN THE FOLLOWING COMMAND
#
# ---
# git rm --cached '**/*.inlang/.gitignore'
# ---
#
# 2. COMMIT THE CHANGE
#
# ---
# git commit -m "fix: remove tracked .gitignore from inlang project"
# ---
#
# Inlang handles the gitignore itself starting with version ^2.5.
#
# everything is ignored except settings.json
*
!settings.json
# ...and except the compiler options. `astro.config.mjs` imports
# paraglide.options.js, so a clone without it cannot build, and the standalone
# `paraglide compile` reads paraglide.config.js to get the same values — if either
# is missing, the CLI silently falls back to Paraglide's defaults and generates a
# runtime that disagrees with the one the bundler ships.
!paraglide.config.js
!paraglide.options.js